  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "For production servers, basic authentication poses a security risk in that username/password gets persisted to a configuration file and/or must be entered as a command line argument.  A better solution for production use of import/export would be certificate authentication.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Presumably this would require:",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "1. ability to enter client_cert and client_key params pointing to location of those items locally",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "2. persist the path to the cert/key as part of the config file so it can be used by the verification tool or when import/export is re-run.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
   "type": "doc",
   "version": 1
  },
